  "language_probability": 1.0,
  "text": "So I started doing a crazy amount of research. I must have read thirty articles, forums, medical breakdowns, all of it. And then I came across a gastroenterologist who explained exactly what GLP-1s do to the gut. He explained it like this: Your stomach is basically a muscle that contracts and pushes everything forward. But GLP-1s slow those contractions down. Think of a river slowing to a trickle. Everything behind it starts to back up, food, waste, gas with nowhere to go. And all that pressure is what you're feeling every day. It wasn't a diet problem, and it wasn't something I was doing wrong. It was the gut slowdown. And my mind started racing. Was this why the fiber never did anything? Why MiraLAX only worked until it wore off? So now I knew what was causing it, but I had no idea what actually fixed the slowdown",
